-- title:
--   Siegel units and modular function fields in Laurent series
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$. Everything takes place inside the field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_q)(\!(t)\!)$ of formal Laurent series over `CyclotomicField q ℚ`, where the variable plays the role of $q^{1/q}$, a uniformiser of width $q$ at the cusp. `zetaQ q` is the distinguished primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ of the cyclotomic field (with `isPrimitiveRoot_zetaQ`, `zetaQ_pow`), and `zetaSubring q` is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta]$ it generates. `jLevel q` is the Laurent series obtained from the expansion `jq` of $j$ by pushing coefficients into $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_q)$ and substituting $t\mapsto t^{q}$, and `jLevelN q d` applies a further substitution $t\mapsto t^{d}$; for $d=1$ the two agree.
--
--   For $a=(a_0,a_1)\in(\mathbb{Z}/q)^2$, with $a_i$ replaced by their representatives in $[0,q)$, one sets $\mathrm{siegelExponent}=6a_0^2-6qa_0+q^2\in\mathbb{Z}$ and $\mathrm{siegelConstExponent}=6a_0a_1$. The power series `siegelSeriesInt q a` over $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta]$ is
--   $$(1-\zeta^{a_1}X^{a_0})\Big(\prod_{n\ge 0}(1-\zeta^{a_1}X^{q(n+1)+a_0})\Big)\Big(\prod_{n\ge 0}(1-\zeta^{q-a_1}X^{q(n+1)-a_0})\Big),$$
--   the products converging coefficientwise; `multipliable_one_sub_C_mul_X_pow` gives multipliability of any family $1-cX^{m(n)}$ with $n<m(n)$, over a commutative ring with an arbitrary topology, and the two instances are checked. Its image `siegelSeries q a` over $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_q)$ has all coefficients in $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta]$, and `siegelPower q a` is $\zeta^{6a_0a_1}t^{6a_0^2-6qa_0+q^2}\cdot(\text{siegelSeries})^{12q}$, the expansion of the $12q$-th power of the Siegel function attached to $a$.
--
--   For $M'\in\mathbb{N}$, `levelGenerators q M'` consists of the constant $\zeta$, the series `jLevelN q d` for nonzero $d\mid M'$, and the substitutions $t\mapsto t^{d}$ of `siegelPower q a` for nonzero $d\mid M'$ and $a\ne 0$; `levelFunctionField q M'` is the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_q)(\!(t)\!)/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by them. It is monotone for divisibility of $M'$, and substitution $t\mapsto t^{\ell}$ carries it into level $M'\ell$. Auxiliary items: `diagD d hd`, the element $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ for $d$ coprime to $q$, with its explicit inverse; `coprime_of_dvd_level`, that $d\mid M'$ and $q\nmid M'$ force $\gcd(d,q)=1$; and `levelComponentField`, which for a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra field $L$ and a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota:\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_q)\to L$ is the intermediate field of $L(\!(t)\!)/L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `levelFunctionField q M'`.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib supplies the cyclotomic field and its distinguished root of unity, and the coefficientwise product topology on power series used for the infinite products; the Siegel-unit expansions, the level generators and the resulting intermediate fields of a Laurent series field are the project's own, built on the substitution homomorphism `qExpand` and the coefficient map `coeffMap` of the imported modules.
--
--   **Where it is used.** These intermediate fields give a concrete model, inside a field of formal Laurent series at the cusp, of the function field of a modular curve with level structure, together with the degeneracy substitutions $t\mapsto t^{\ell}$ relating different levels and the diagonal matrices $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$; the Siegel units provide the extra generators beyond the $j$-expansions.
